# {{FH_PROJECT}} workflow (canonical)

The single source of truth for how a {{FH_ARTIFACT_NOUN}} moves through gates.
`SKILL.md` only points here; never duplicate this content elsewhere.

Every command below runs from the project root, with the venv from `make venv`:
`PY=.venv/bin/python`, `GATE="$PY harness/core/cli/gate.py"`.

## Lifecycle

1. Start a unit: `$GATE start --unit <slug>`. The unit lives in `{{FH_UNIT_DIR}}/<slug>/`.
2. Attempt the gate the unit waits at: `$GATE attempt <gate> --unit <slug>`. Gates advance
   **in order**; `$GATE status --unit <slug>` says which gate is next.
3. When a gate waits for a human, `$GATE pending --unit <slug>` shows the request. The answer
   is `$GATE proceed --unit <slug> --decision approve --by <name>` (tty approvals must be given
   from a terminal; token approvals need the token printed when the request was raised).
4. A unit ends in a terminal state: the sealing gate, or `escalated` (with a written "why I am
   stuck" note: `$GATE escalate --unit <slug> --note <text>`). Never ship confidently wrong work.
5. `$GATE verify --unit <slug>` proves the evidence chain of a unit (read only).

## Gate chain

{{FH_GATE_CHAIN}}

The last gate seals the unit. Each gate's checks read the unit's files; a fatal finding
(including a deny policy in `harness/adapter/adapter.yaml`) fails the attempt and the gate
stays where it is.
